Z||000000||RiceCooker||07-31-2001||03:01 PM||||Hey neighbors! How's it goin? Any plans for the long weekend?<P>I finally got some holidays from work and I've been planning to come out for quite some time. <BR>I'm leaving bright and early tomorrow morning (Wednesday) and I'll be in Langley by sunset. I'm staying in Langley for a week then heading back out to Armstrong (close to Vernon) for a couple days before i head home. <BR>I would like to know if anyone wants to meet up. I wanna check out some sweet BC fieros and maybe hang out.<BR>I'm coming out mostly to visit my Aunt & Uncle in Langley so I dont have too much else planned. I'll be bringing my golf clubs, my guitar my hackey sack, and my beer (among other things) Anybody here golf?<BR>Wish me luck on my drive and talk to ya soon<P>Todd<P>Cool! 500!<p>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||BC-GT||07-31-2001||03:38 PM||||Sounds good, you should try to get to the Sea-to-Sky Highway that goes up to Whistler. It was made for the Fiero and one beautiful drive to boot. If you want to golf while you are up there you could check out Furry Creek. Played there a few years back, very nice, plays into the mountains, then winds back down to the ocean. Here's a pic from one of the tee boxes. <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pb7dfd8c1a6a6b010868a1f4eec4f9c0d/fe521089.jpg.orig.jpg"> kinda pricey though.<BR>By the way, I have an old Hackey sack here that was brought back from the Phillipine Islands over 20 years ago, probably one of the first ones in Canada<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||07-31-2001||04:15 PM||||Thanks Darryl. Whereabouts is Furry Creek? It looks absolutley stunning and indeed quite pricey. I'm not lookin to spend more than $60 on green fees. Also I don't want to go to the strictest place. (sshhhh, i dont even have golf shoes) I just golf in my Nikes and dress up a bit but i shoot low 90's which is okay since ive only been golfing for about 4 years. <BR>So you live in Burnaby, eh? Maybe we can call up Joey Sakic and see if he wants to go for a round of golf.<BR>Is there a Vancouver or BC fiero club that might be up to something? <P>Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||BC-GT||07-31-2001||04:35 PM||||Furry Creek is right on the Sea-to-Sky highway right around Squamish.(30-40 minutes outside of North Vancouver) There is a club here but I'm not in it yet and a lot of there links are not updated but here is a link to the originator of it. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html</A>   His name is David. I believe they meet on Saturdays in Surrey, but not sure which Saturday(once a month)<BR> Not real sure of the cost of most golf courses here, don't get out that much anymore. I did however golf in Washington just over the line in the middle of February!! in a t-shirt(how cool is that, I'm originally from the Peg.) costs 17 bucks Canadian for that one. Furry Creek would be closer to $75-$100 I would think, a cart is mandatory given the conditions||||reg||1
